%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Skuldafn
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d0c7e6e02081ef145a5f9d29590789ea, type: 2}
    dialog: This is far as I can take you. Krif voth ahkrin.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988565371781159
    - rid: 4927988565371781160
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d0c7e6e02081ef145a5f9d29590789ea, type: 2}
    dialog: I will look for your return, or Alduin's.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988590059192372
    - rid: 4927988590059192373
    - rid: 4927988590059192374
    - rid: 4927988590059192377
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: With his final scripted remarks out of the way, Odahviing flies off to...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Somewhere else, I guess.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: It's possible he's heading up to the Throat of the World, since he's
      there for the ending sequence.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Not that it matters to me right now, I've a portal to enter.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: If I remember right, this place is a doozy, even for characters that
      are properly leveled.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: And I'm pretty sure that if I <i>could</i> check, I would be seriously
      underleveled.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Also, I'm still rocking the armor I got from Helgen.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: All in all? My odds are pretty bad.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: At least I know the level layout!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Since that's the only thing I've got going for me, I should probably
      just try to sneak or run past the enemies.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Except for the Dragon Priest waiting for me at the end...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Meh! I'll cross that bridge when I get there!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: First, I need to sneak past that draugr patrolling the ramparts.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'll let him do his path for a bit...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599478
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Okay, based on his movements, I should be able to sneak up to the right
      side of the second arch.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Once there, I can wait for him to move his way to the left...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: And while he's facing the other direction I can sneak behind that pillar...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599424
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Up those stairs is an elevated platform with a handful of draugr guarding
      it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Unfortunately, it's very wide open; no room to hide.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: There's nothing from stopping me climbing up that cliff face to my right,
      is there?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Other than wonky Skyrim collisions, which isn't exactly a problem for
      a person that actually has function limbs and isn't just a character controller.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, let's see if I can get a good grip...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599480
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Minor inconveniences aside, this should be doable...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright, I'm up.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599481
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: And behind a conveniently placed decorative pillar.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I got a good view from up here...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Ah! I should be able to drop down to the entrance of the temple from
      up here.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: How will I get there unnoticed...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Since there's no draugr up here, I should be able to make it over by
      going prone and crawling...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Temple entrance in sight... guarded by a draugr wight.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599482
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Phooey.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: He's just standing around...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Hm. What can I even do...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: There's this big pile of rubble in front of me, with some loose rocks
      that'd be easy enough to throw...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I might be able to distract him by throwing it...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: But, there's also these weird trench thingies to the sides of the stairs...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Why are they even here?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... maybe they used to be some sort of water fixture?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Not that their purpose matters to me; I might be able to use one of them
      to go prone again...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Plan concocted!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I throw the rock to get him looking to my right, then use the time afforded
      to get in position at the leftmost trench.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Skyrim NPCs usually take their time investigating sounds, so I should
      be able to sneak my way up the trench.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Even if he does turn around, I should be slightly covered up by the trench...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Alright here goes nothing...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Rock thrown...!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599483
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: The draugr is investigating where the rock fell...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: And we're in!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 4927988638874599484
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I'm doing pretty good so far.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
